<!-- INTRO -->
<div class="intro">
  <div class="intro-main">
    <p>The Filter is a <strong>prioritization and delivery governance system</strong> — a structured way for your leadership team to agree on what gets worked on first, confirm it's being delivered, and say no to everything that doesn't make the cut.</p>
    <p>This engagement installs the system, runs the first live forums, and trains your internal operator to run it themselves. By the final week, they're facilitating with me in a supporting role — and once the four weeks are done, the process is theirs.</p>
    <p>The goal isn't dependency. <strong>It's transfer.</strong> By the time I leave, your team runs this without me.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="intro-facts">
    <div class="fact-row">
      <span class="fact-label">Duration</span>
      <span class="fact-value">4 Weeks</span>
    </div>
    <div class="fact-row">
      <span class="fact-label">Format</span>
      <span class="fact-value">Remote (on-site option Wk 2)</span>
    </div>
    <div class="fact-row">
      <span class="fact-label">Your time commitment</span>
      <span class="fact-value">~10 hrs total (~2.5/week)</span>
    </div>
    <div class="fact-row">
      <span class="fact-label">Decision Authority</span>
      <span class="fact-value">CEO / COO / Founder</span>
    </div>
    <div class="fact-row">
      <span class="fact-label">Internal Operator</span>
      <span class="fact-value">Assigned by you, trained by me</span>
    </div>
    <div class="fact-row">
      <span class="fact-label">Investment</span>
      <span class="fact-value">$35,000 (remote) · $42,000 (on-site)</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- SPONSORSHIP -->
<div class="sponsorship">
  <div class="sponsorship-label">Week 1 — Decision Authority Sponsorship</div>
  <p>This engagement only works if the leadership team believes the system has real authority behind it. <strong>Week 1 begins with a sponsorship statement from you</strong> — the Decision Authority — delivered to the full team before the intake opens.</p>
  <p style="margin-top:0.75rem;">The message is simple: this is how we're going to make decisions going forward. Everything goes through the intake. The ranked list guides the forum. And when the system says something isn't first — we hold that, even when it's uncomfortable.</p>
  <div class="sponsorship-note">Without visible sponsorship from the top, the system becomes optional. With it, it becomes the standard.</div>
</div>

<!-- WEEK BY WEEK -->
<div class="weeks">
  <div class="weeks-title">Week by Week</div>

  <div class="week">
    <div class="week-num">
      <span class="week-num-label">Week</span>
      <span class="week-num-val">1</span>
    </div>
    <div class="week-content">
      <div class="week-name">Foundation & Intake</div>
      <div class="week-desc">I introduce the system, the rules, and the goal of the engagement to the full team. We cover the difference between BAU operations and improvement initiatives — and why that distinction matters. Everyone receives the intake form and is assigned homework: document every active improvement initiative plus known backlog items. Office hours are held 2 days later for anyone who needs support completing their submission. <strong>The internal operator is named before this session begins</strong> — they attend everything from day one and we hold our first 1:1 this week to align on their role.</div>
      <div class="week-items">
        <span class="week-item">Team kickoff</span>
        <span class="week-item">Sponsorship statement</span>
        <span class="week-item">Intake form distributed</span>
        <span class="week-item">BAU vs improvement training</span>
        <span class="week-item">Office hours (48hrs later)</span>
        <span class="week-item">Operator named & first 1:1</span>
        <span class="week-item">Decision Authority pre-brief</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="week highlight">
    <div class="week-num">
      <span class="week-num-label">Week</span>
      <span class="week-num-val">2</span>
    </div>
    <div class="week-content">
      <div class="week-name">The Main Event — Portfolio Baseline</div>
      <div class="week-desc">This is the most important session of the engagement. The full initiative list is on the table. We open with 45 minutes of quiet reading time — everyone absorbs the full picture before anyone speaks. Then each initiative gets 1–3 minutes: owner presents, team reacts, score is reviewed. The goal is one clear outcome: <strong>kill at least one initiative that shouldn't exist.</strong> Even one. That moment proves the system has teeth. On-site option available for this week — I come to you for 2 days and run the workshop live. Operator 1:1 after the session to debrief.</div>
      <div class="week-items">
        <span class="week-item">45-min quiet read</span>
        <span class="week-item">Full portfolio review</span>
        <span class="week-item">Score & rank all initiatives</span>
        <span class="week-item">Kill at least one</span>
        <span class="week-item">Capacity check</span>
        <span class="week-item">On-site option available</span>
        <span class="week-item">Operator 1:1 debrief</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="week">
    <div class="week-num">
      <span class="week-num-label">Week</span>
      <span class="week-num-val">3</span>
    </div>
    <div class="week-content">
      <div class="week-name">Operator Takes the Room</div>
      <div class="week-desc">This is the first forum your operator runs — not me. Before the call, we meet to prep: I walk them through the agenda, and we anticipate and rehearse the moments that test a system early — the first attempt to route around intake, a low-value item nobody wants to kill, a score someone challenges. During the forum, they facilitate and I'm in the room supporting — stepping in only if needed, so the team starts seeing them as the authority, not me. After, we debrief 1:1: what worked, what felt hard, what to adjust. The session itself should be deliberately boring — status on active work, new intake reviewed against the scoring model, a capacity check before anything new gets activated.</div>
      <div class="week-items">
        <span class="week-item">Pre-forum prep & rehearsal</span>
        <span class="week-item">Operator facilitates</span>
        <span class="week-item">I support in the room</span>
        <span class="week-item">Active status + new intake</span>
        <span class="week-item">Post-forum 1:1 debrief</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="week">
    <div class="week-num">
      <span class="week-num-label">Week</span>
      <span class="week-num-val">4</span>
    </div>
    <div class="week-content">
      <div class="week-name">Full Handoff + Demos</div>
      <div class="week-desc">Same model — I prep the operator beforehand, they run the full forum, I support from the side. By the end of this session they've facilitated start to finish in front of the team with me there as the safety net, so the first time they face a hard moment alone isn't after I'm gone. This forum adds demos: teams show work that's live or nearly live, with adoption and rollout planning. We close with the final 1:1 — debrief the call, resolve any open questions, confirm they have everything they need. The keys are fully transferred.</div>
      <div class="week-items">
        <span class="week-item">Pre-forum prep</span>
        <span class="week-item">Operator runs full forum</span>
        <span class="week-item">I support in the room</span>
        <span class="week-item">Live demos & rollout</span>
        <span class="week-item">Final 1:1 & formal handoff</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="week" style="border-top:3px solid var(--maroon);">
    <div class="week-num" style="background:var(--off-black);">
      <span class="week-num-label" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);">After</span>
      <span class="week-num-val" style="color:var(--white);font-size:1.5rem;">Wk 4</span>
    </div>
    <div class="week-content">
      <div class="week-name">The System Is Yours</div>
      <div class="week-desc">The four weeks are done and I'm out. Your operator runs the forum independently — the system, the rules, the cadence, and the full documentation all belong to your team. I'm available for a 30-minute check-in at 30 and 60 days if you want one. After that, you have everything you need to run this indefinitely.</div>
      <div class="week-items">
        <span class="week-item">Operator fully independent</span>
        <span class="week-item">30 & 60-day check-ins available</span>
        <span class="week-item">Full documentation retained</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>

